{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1119799-just-how-strong-encompassing-is-quiescence-in-your-games","id":1119799,"title":"Just how strong / encompassing is Quiescence in your games?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-24T01:00:09-07:00","id":1119799,"title":"Just how strong / encompassing is Quiescence in your games?","content":"Mage 2E in its chapter Through Awakened Eyes mentions a lake that, deep enough, leads to vast underground tunnels and seas and is inhabitated by alien creatures. It also mentions a diver who is snatched by the weird inhabitants there and then tells us that authorities and human society at large do not find the body and only come up with mundane speculations. Just how does this work? Do they conduct a thorough search with divers in the lake and the collective quiescence simply causes them to ignore or instantly forget the labyrinths and creatures that they should logically find? Do the Exarchs / Guardians of the Veil / The God-Machine send their agents to clean it all up and wipe memories?<br /> <br /> Quiescence, the mechanics to explain exactly why the facade of normalty does not immediately burst in this game, is by far the hardest challenge for me. I always have a hard time all the puzzle pieces that keeps this flimsy masquerade together. I hope I can get some more understanding by talking about it here.<br /> <br /> Also, just how far does quiescence go the more indirect a character's actions are? My understanding is that if a mage hurls a fireball in a crowded street the witnesses would rationalize it as a gas explosion or maybe a terrorist attack. But what if a mage would slaughter an entire village by making their bodies melt or exploding their heads? Would quiescence kick in then as well, making investigators simply deny all supernatural explanations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T03:28:13-07:00","id":1119824,"title":"","content":"For the deep lake, the &quot;thorough search&quot; might have only searched the shallows near the coast. The divers avoiding the deeper parts instinctivly as soon as they start seeing wierdness. Rationalising not going there as &quot;its been searched already/someone else will do it&quot;.<br /> <br /> People in a village melting would be harder to explain away. Acidic gas? Sudden agressive flesh eating baceria? Any explanation that makes the government quarantine the area as way to dangerous would work.<br /> <br /> My headcanon is the God-Machine fixes a lot of things behind the scenes and keeps people away, but will avoid attracting nosy mages. So it will stop supressing wierd stuff and remove traces of itself if it detects mages investigating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T03:51:47-07:00","id":1119827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do they conduct a thorough search with divers in the lake and the collective quiescence simply causes them to ignore or instantly forget the labyrinths and creatures that they should logically find </div> </div> </div>Basically, yeah. I mean, they might report back that there are tunnels or ruins at the bottom of the lake, but if there's no plausible way to report it, the sleeper will just blank it from memory. Most of the time at least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do the Exarchs / Guardians of the Veil / The God-Machine send their agents to clean it all up and wipe memories? </div> </div> </div>Quite possibly, but they don't need to wipe memories, the majority of people don't want to know. These things cause integrity breaks, they're literally harmful on a spiritual level. It's probably enough to give sleepers a good reason not to go near the things that cause them pain.<br /> <br /> The chapter you want to understand the Quiescence is the sleeper section of Supporting Cast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T08:27:49-07:00","id":1119882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RBAWintrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1119799-just-how-strong-encompassing-is-quiescence-in-your-games?p=1119824#post1119824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My headcanon is the God-Machine fixes a lot of things behind the scenes and keeps people away, but will avoid attracting nosy mages. So it will stop supressing wierd stuff and remove traces of itself if it detects mages investigating.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have used the GM for exactly the same purposes, making it do all kinds of work in secret to keep the facade from cracking. I am not sure how I would have explained it without such a powerful entity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T08:29:55-07:00","id":1119883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1119799-just-how-strong-encompassing-is-quiescence-in-your-games?p=1119827#post1119827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Basically, yeah. I mean, they might report back that there are tunnels or ruins at the bottom of the lake, but if there's no plausible way to report it, the sleeper will just blank it from memory. Most of the time at least.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Quite possibly, but they don't need to wipe memories, the majority of people don't want to know. These things cause integrity breaks, they're literally harmful on a spiritual level. It's probably enough to give sleepers a good reason not to go near the things that cause them pain.<br /> <br /> The chapter you want to understand the Quiescence is the sleeper section of Supporting Cast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you much, I will make sure to read that section more thoroughly then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T08:36:31-07:00","id":1119889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1119799-just-how-strong-encompassing-is-quiescence-in-your-games?p=1119882#post1119882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have used the GM for exactly the same purposes, making it do all kinds of work in secret to keep the facade from cracking. I am not sure how I would have explained it without such a powerful entity.</div> </div> </div> </div>For all intents and purposes, the God Machine's processes are natural, yet hyper scientific. Supernal magic fucks people up in such an unnatural fashion that it creates fugues, obsessions, and an infinite list of psychological derangements.<br /> <br /> There wouldn't be anything wrong with trying to enforce say, a Masquerade for magic in your own setting if that's more your thing. In fact, it'd make Hunters more of an issue for Mages.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T08:49:41-07:00","id":1119897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1119799-just-how-strong-encompassing-is-quiescence-in-your-games?p=1119889#post1119889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For all intents and purposes, the God Machine's processes are natural, yet hyper scientific. Supernal magic fucks people up in such an unnatural fashion that it creates fugues, obsessions, and an infinite list of psychological derangements.<br /> <br /> There wouldn't be anything wrong with trying to enforce say, a Masquerade for magic in your own setting if that's more your thing. In fact, it'd make Hunters more of an issue for Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. An easy hack is to make it like Lunacy, in that many forget, some remember (traumatically), and some can deal with it (or get transformed). It is mildly self managing, but Mages are still encouraged to keep it under wraps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T12:18:19-07:00","id":1119992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1119799-just-how-strong-encompassing-is-quiescence-in-your-games?p=1119889#post1119889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For all intents and purposes, the God Machine's processes are natural, yet hyper scientific. Supernal magic fucks people up in such an unnatural fashion that it creates fugues, obsessions, and an infinite list of psychological derangements.<br /> <br /> There wouldn't be anything wrong with trying to enforce say, a Masquerade for magic in your own setting if that's more your thing. In fact, it'd make Hunters more of an issue for Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, interesting! I can certainly consider this idea, though it would necessarily tone down the amount of fantasy in my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","user":"Aristarkos","date":". 07-24-2017, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T15:54:08-07:00","id":1120112,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> had great 'house rule' for running Quiescence - instead any Sleeper seeing Supernal would try to make most bland and common explanation - Sleeper just go deeper in to his beliefs. Christian seeing magic thinks about miracle - or works of Devil. Conspiracy Theorist see 'riptalian technology', etc. He maybe so much shocked he will not try to talk about it more - or spread massage in closed circles ( like conspiracy theory magazines ). Seeing magic <i>changes</i> Sleeper, even when he want to explain to him in other way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T03:50:08-07:00","id":1120288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1119799-just-how-strong-encompassing-is-quiescence-in-your-games?p=1120112#post1120112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> had great 'house rule' for running Quiescence - instead any Sleeper seeing Supernal would try to make most bland and common explanation - Sleeper just go deeper in to his beliefs. Christian seeing magic thinks about miracle - or works of Devil. Conspiracy Theorist see 'riptalian technology', etc. He maybe so much shocked he will not try to talk about it more - or spread massage in closed circles ( like conspiracy theory magazines ). Seeing magic <i>changes</i> Sleeper, even when he want to explain to him in other way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes me wonder what happens when a agnostic witnesses magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T04:00:38-07:00","id":1120291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1119799-just-how-strong-encompassing-is-quiescence-in-your-games?p=1120288#post1120288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Makes me wonder what happens when a agnostic witnesses magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>He goes 'Magic? No, it's nonsense - it must more to it...' - and start to purse the Awakened PCs to uncover 'THE TRUTH'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T04:25:40-07:00","id":1120304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1119799-just-how-strong-encompassing-is-quiescence-in-your-games?p=1120291#post1120291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He goes 'Magic? No, it's nonsense - it must more to it...' - and start to purse the Awakened PCs to uncover 'THE TRUTH'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agnosticism isn't the denial of the supernatural, merely the Socratic approach to it (&quot;I understand that I'm wholy unprepared to comprehend what just happened and Im far better off without trying to understand it&quot;.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T07:07:07-07:00","id":1120341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1119799-just-how-strong-encompassing-is-quiescence-in-your-games?p=1120304#post1120304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agnosticism isn't the denial of the supernatural, merely the Socratic approach to it (&quot;I understand that I'm wholy unprepared to comprehend what just happened and Im far better off without trying to understand it&quot;.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's personally how I choose to run it, as something <i>way </i>above the average Sleeper's pay grade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T09:31:04-07:00","id":1120380,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9849_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9849\" data-vbnamecard=\"9849\">Aristarkos</a> i am confuse, are you asking how each of us manage Quiessence in our games or how the setting/mechanic says the situations you propose are to be handle by Quiessence?<br /> <br /> How i handle it in my games? I follow the Dresden files route and remove Quiessence from my games/setting but i also have 0 interest in the whole &quot;world is prision&quot; and other cosmic/existencial concerns. <br /> <br /> So it boils down to <i>&quot;We're ostriches, and the whole world is sand. Newbies who are just learning about the world of wizards and the unpleasant side of the supernatural always think there's this huge conspiracy to hide it from everyone. There isn't. There's no need for one, beyond preventing actual parades down Main Street. Hell's bells, from where I'm standing, it's a miracle anyone </i><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">ever</span></span><i> notices.&quot;<br /> <br /> As for the rules as written people have put it better than i could.</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T11:59:12-07:00","id":1120439,"title":"","content":"The masquerade's first defense is simple lack of interest. Most witnesses, if it doesn't impact them directly, will think &quot;that's interesting&quot;, then go on about their business.<br /> Second is humanity's astounding ability to rationalize things away, especially when they don't bother to look deeper.<br /> Last but certainly not least is social pressure. People who claim to see UFOs are open to public ridicule, their stories mocked not investigated.<br /> <br /> \u200bIn my games there are two primary reasons Mages don't go large in public: Fear of Guardians, Seers and Banishers taking an interest in them and knowledge that witnessing Magic is a breaking point that can harm the people around them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T13:08:35-07:00","id":1120459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1119799-just-how-strong-encompassing-is-quiescence-in-your-games?p=1120380#post1120380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> i am confuse, are you asking how each of us manage Quiessence in our games or how the setting/mechanic says the situations you propose are to be handle by Quiessence?<br /> <br /> How i handle it in my games? I follow the Dresden files route and remove Quiessence from my games/setting but i also have 0 interest in the whole &amp;quot;world is prision&amp;quot; and other cosmic/existencial concerns. <br /> <br /> So it boils down to <i>&amp;quot;We're ostriches, and the whole world is sand. Newbies who are just learning about the world of wizards and the unpleasant side of the supernatural always think there's this huge conspiracy to hide it from everyone. There isn't. There's no need for one, beyond preventing actual parades down Main Street. Hell's bells, from where I'm standing, it's a miracle anyone </i><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">ever</span></span><i> notices.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> As for the rules as written people have put it better than i could.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I wanted first and foremost to know how others handle it and how they think about it. I sort of understand what the book is going for, but it is nice to get some ideas and clarification from how others have approached it. I have gotten lots of great input already, yours amongst them, so I am thankful for that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T01:58:50-07:00","id":1120705,"title":"","content":"Is Quiescence only tied directly to supernal phenomena or other supernatural entities as well? The book seems a bit vague at that point.<br /> <br /> Does Quiescence activate when sleepers encounter...<br /> Cryptids?<br /> Ghosts?<br /> God-Machine servitors?<br /> Vampiric Disciplines?<br /> Mage servitors such as Eidolons and Golems?<br /> Any kind of supernatural occurence, really?<br /> <br /> How can Hunter: the Vigil even be a gameline if Quiescence goes into all this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T02:31:09-07:00","id":1120709,"title":"","content":"It's tied directly to Supernal phenomenon, and Mages suspect that it's indirectly responsible for helping maintain the secrecy of non-Supernal phenomenon as well by maintaining the attitude of not wanting to know in those subject to the Lie.<br /> <br /> Most Hunters are pretty much a non-issue for Mages, but other splats don't share the same level of inherent protection.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, Hunter works perfectly well as its own game line. It's meant to be run by itself on its own rules, and so are all the other game lines. Ever since cWoD though people have wanted crossover, but back then it was a mess since it was an unexpected desire from players. nWod and CoD streamlines it for if you insist on having crossover, but it's still not the intention of any of the game lines (Except Beast) which is why they are not balanced out against each other at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 07-26-2017, 05:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T03:37:38-07:00","id":1120722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1119799-just-how-strong-encompassing-is-quiescence-in-your-games?p=1120705#post1120705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Quiescence only tied directly to supernal phenomena or other supernatural entities as well? The book seems a bit vague at that point.<br /> <br /> Does Quiescence activate when sleepers encounter...<br /> Cryptids?<br /> Ghosts?<br /> God-Machine servitors?<br /> Vampiric Disciplines?<br /> Mage servitors such as Eidolons and Golems?<br /> Any kind of supernatural occurence, really?<br /> <br /> How can Hunter: the Vigil even be a gameline if Quiescence goes into all this?</div> </div> </div> </div>In order: No, no, no, hah! no, probably and probably. <br /> <br /> The specific methods by which each of the negatives above occlude their existance varies from Infrastructure, to tactics that indulge facades of normalcy such as the Masquerade or plain infiltrated cell tactics.<br /> <br /> Most Endowed Hunters do not suffer Quiescence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 07-26-2017, 06:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T04:13:42-07:00","id":1120739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1119799-just-how-strong-encompassing-is-quiescence-in-your-games?p=1120705#post1120705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> How can Hunter: the Vigil even be a gameline if Quiescence goes into all this?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Anything with a &quot;supernatural&quot; merit is considered a sleepwalker and immune to Quiescence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T04:40:42-07:00","id":1120744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1119799-just-how-strong-encompassing-is-quiescence-in-your-games?p=1120739#post1120739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything with a &amp;quot;supernatural&amp;quot; merit is considered a sleepwalker and immune to Quiescence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if the merit is inherent to the person, you count as a Sleepwalker if you're psychic, but you don't if your powers come from a ring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T10:21:06-07:00","id":1121370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1119799-just-how-strong-encompassing-is-quiescence-in-your-games?p=1120705#post1120705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can Hunter: the Vigil even be a gameline if Quiescence goes into all this?</div> </div> </div> </div>As has been said above, being a Sleepwalker is a thing, so some of them are immune to it outright. Also, Quiescence is only ever ironclad when it comes to Supernal stuff. While it subtly conditions people to ignore the other supernatural phenomenon it isn't nearly as heavy handed, so someone truly dedicated to finding (or traumatized by) non-Supernal supernatural stuff can still manage to do so, which is why Hunter works in setting.<br /> <br /> It's also why its been said that Hunter isn't really much of an issue when it comes to Mage, because Supernal magic forces a hard NO on any non-Sleepwalker trying to deal with anything Supernal (as well as the general power gap between lines for those that are immune).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T11:44:44-07:00","id":1121430,"title":"","content":"I figured that a Hunter who has started on a Vigil is a legit quasi supernatural thing. Even if it seems normal, I've always interpreted the Vigil as being something akin to what happens to the progenitors who created the first Prometheans of a Lineage. It's mundane-ish and can be explained away but is still supernatural in an underhanded way. So I wouldn't think they (or Slashers for that matter) would suffer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T21:20:11-07:00","id":1121703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1119799-just-how-strong-encompassing-is-quiescence-in-your-games?p=1121430#post1121430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figured that a Hunter who has started on a Vigil is a legit quasi supernatural thing. Even if it seems normal, I've always interpreted the Vigil as being something akin to what happens to the progenitors who created the first Prometheans of a Lineage. It's mundane-ish and can be explained away but is still supernatural in an underhanded way. So I wouldn't think they (or Slashers for that matter) would suffer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, unfortunately, assuming it isn't something that is changing in 2e, Hunters are purely non-supernatural. At least they are at base. They <i>can</i> individually have things like Endowments or other supernatural merits that would give them Sleepwalker status.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T10:38:28-07:00","id":1121953,"title":"","content":"I am still deeply confused but that's ok. Quiescence is tied directly to supernal phenomena (i.e. The stuff mages do), not to every single supernatural instance, and even then only to the obvously supernatural stuff? Is that the final call on this? It still creates much uncertainty for me where to exactly draw the line if it would be Quiescence or not. How about the following examples?<br /> <br /> Cryptids, no.<br /> Transformed shark-wolf hybrid using Life Arcana, yes.<br /> <br /> Weird superscience prototype robot, no.<br /> Mage golem looking like a Hellenistic statue, yes.<br /> Mage golem looking like weird superscience prototype robot, no.<br /> <br /> Platypus, no.<br /> Transformed duck-boar hybrid using Life, yes.<br /> <br /> Spirit of Sadness materilized as a black cloud with tears as raindrops, no.<br /> Spirit of Sadness made by Spirit Arcana to materialize as a giant moving smiling flower instead, yes.<br /> <br /> Witnessing vampire with Celerity rush past, no.<br /> Witnessing mage with Acceleration rush past, yes.<br /> <br /> Werewolf in Urhan (simple wolf) form starts to talk, no.<br /> Ordinary wolf starts to talk due to Life Arcana, yes.<br /> <br /> All of the above should probably prompt a Breaking Point roll with me as a GM (not platypus, maybe) but while Breaking Points are painful to a Mortal it does not really trigger the &quot;ignore and forget&quot; effect that Quiescence has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","user":"Aristarkos","date":". 07-28-2017, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T10:48:04-07:00","id":1121957,"title":"","content":"It's a pretty easy division, &quot;Is it made by Supernal magic and also obviously magical?&quot; If yes then Quiesence, if no then no Quiesence. I don't know how you're not getting that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T10:57:16-07:00","id":1121962,"title":"","content":"1. Sleeper sees supernatural phenomenon.<br /> 2. Goes &quot;Oh, shi-&quot;<br /> 3. Shard if Abyss wakes up, looks around.<br /> 4. Sees Supernal magic.<br /> 5. Triggers Dissonance/Disbelief/Quiesence.<br /> <br /> Not obvious? Stop before 1. Not Supernal? Abyssal shard goes back to sleep after 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T12:58:56-07:00","id":1122021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1119799-just-how-strong-encompassing-is-quiescence-in-your-games?p=1121962#post1121962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Sleeper sees supernatural phenomenon.<br /> 2. Goes &amp;quot;Oh, shi-&amp;quot;<br /> 3. Shard if Abyss wakes up, looks around.<br /> 4. Sees Supernal magic.<br /> 5. Triggers Dissonance/Disbelief/Quiesence.<br /> <br /> Not obvious? Stop before 1. Not Supernal? Abyssal shard goes back to sleep after 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really tempted to make an actual flowchart of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}